Two or more of these clinical features establish the diagnosis:  Two or more of these clinical features establish the diagnosis:  •    Six or more café au lait spots (macules or patches). Numbers increase in childhood. Spots in prepubertal children $>5m m$ in diameter, but post-puberty $>15mathrm{mm}$ . Usually have smooth outlines, but larger ones may be irregular. Intensity of colour varies, but most are pale brown. Fade in adulthood. •    Six or more café au lait spots (macules or patches). Numbers increase in childhood. Spots in prepubertal children $>5m m$ in diameter, but post-puberty $>15\mathrm{mm}$ . Usually have smooth outlines, but larger ones may be irregular. Intensity of colour varies, but most are pale brown. Fade in adulthood.

